# Open Engineering Playbook CODEOWNERS template for GitLab. Copy to .gitlab/CODEOWNERS.
# Docs: https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/user/project/codeowners/
#
# Rules:
# - Use groups (@group/subgroup), never individuals who might leave.
# - Sections group rules; within a section the last matching pattern wins.
# - [Section][2] requires two approvals from that section's owners.
# - ^[Section] makes a section optional (owners are suggested, not required).
# - Turn on "Require approval from code owners" for the protected branch.
# - Code Owners needs GitLab Premium or Ultimate. On the Free tier GitLab
#   does not use this file: name reviewers on each merge request instead.
# Replace @your-group/... with your own groups.

[Default] @your-group/service-team
*

[Database][2] @your-group/service-team @your-group/data-platform
/migrations/
/db/

[Security][2] @your-group/security-champions
/src/auth/
/src/crypto/

[Infrastructure] @your-group/platform
/infra/
*.tf

[CI and repository rules][2] @your-group/platform @your-group/security-champions
/.gitlab-ci.yml
/.gitlab/
/.gitlab/CODEOWNERS
/AGENTS.md
**/AGENTS.md

^[Documentation] @your-group/tech-writers
/docs/
